{"reference":"1 Kings 9","book":"1 Kings","chapter":9,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Questions of Interpretation","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Verses 1–9 place the completed temple and Davidic dynasty under a warning: neither provides immunity from judgment if Israel turns to other gods. The later accounts of Solomon’s building program, administration, and wealth raise further historical questions. Their scale, chronology, and archaeological profile remain disputed; monumental remains may illuminate Iron Age state formation, but they do not independently establish every attribution made in Kings.","verse_refs":["1 Kings 9:1-9","1 Kings 9:15-28"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_kings_009_1d2b1b726760f1daaa641d25"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}